LongevityOS data licence
========================

The curated corpora in this repository — the evidence atlas (app/js/data.js),
the human-evidence ledger (app/js/evidence.js), the reference set
(app/js/chem/targets.js), the literature feed (data/feed.json) and every
dataset export the project publishes — are released under the

    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may copy, redistribute, remix and build on them for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit ("LongevityOS,
https://github.com/PhotonBounce/longevityos"), link to the licence, and
indicate if changes were made.

Two things this licence does not change:

1. Every row cites a primary source (a PubMed record, a registered trial, a
   PubChem compound). The underlying papers and databases keep their own
   terms; the CC BY licence covers our curation, wording and structure.
2. Nothing here is medical advice. A dataset row describes what a study
   reported in the people it enrolled; it is not a recommendation to anyone.

Third-party data the swarm ingests (PubChem, and in later releases ChEMBL and
DrugAge) carries its own licence, which the ingesting tool records alongside
the data it fetched.

The software itself is under the MIT licence in LICENSE.
